 agree with CB Roger McCreary on 1-year deal","description":"The Lions added free agent cornerback Roger McCreary on a one-year deal, a source told ESPN.","published":"2026-03-13T22:49:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/48199022/lions-agree-cb-roger-mccreary-1-year-deal","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Rams add CB depth with McCreary -- but otherwise hold strong","description":"While this Rams team does have Super Bowl aspirations -- and two first-round picks to make a big acquisition -- they are unlikely to use either to make a splash move.","published":"2025-10-31T14:04:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/46771933/los-angeles-rams-add-cornerback-depth-roger-mccreary-hold-strong-2025-nfl-trade-deadline","type":"Story","byline":"Sarah Barshop","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Rams acquire CB Roger McCreary from Titans with draft pick swap","description":"The Titans traded cornerback Roger McCreary to the Rams for a conditional draft pick swap on Monday.","published":"2025-10-27T18:51:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/46746696/rams-acquire-cb-roger-mccreary-titans-draft-pick-swap","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Sarah Barshop","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"A look at four players that the Tennessee Titans could trade","description":"As the Nov. 4 trade deadline approaches, here are some things Tennessee can do as it looks toward the future.","published":"2025-10-24T10:00:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/46698597/tennessee-titans-trade-deadline-moves-arden-key-calvin-ridley-roger-mccreary","type":"Story","byline":"Turron Davenport","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Titans' McCreary jumps out of bounds to tip interception of Herbert back to Kalu","description":"Kalu's first interception of career comes in highlight fashion for Tennessee.","published":"2022-12-18T23:57:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/35281424/titans-mccreary-jumps-bounds-tip-interception-kalu","type":"Story","byline":"Turron Davenport","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Titans coach Mike Vrabel searching inside (and outside) the building for answers to secondary woes","description":"Vrabel made it clear that they will continue to search to bring guys in midseason if his current crop of defensive backs can't turn things around.","published":"2022-09-27T12:36:07.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/tennessee-titans/post/_/id/32710/titans-coach-mike-vrabel-searching-inside-and-outside-the-building-for-secondary-woes","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Turron Davenport","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Tennessee Titans NFL draft picks 2022: Analysis for every selection","description":"The Titans selected Arkansas wide receiver Treylon Burks with the No. 18 pick in the NFL draft.","published":"2022-04-28T21:05:38.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/tennessee-titans/post/_/id/32331/tennessee-titans-nfl-draft-picks-2022-analysis-for-every-selection","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Turron Davenport","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"How the Buffalo Bills can address cornerback in bid to maintain No. 1 defense","description":"The Bills haven't tried to solve their issues at cornerback yet this offseason, but they still have intriguing options in the draft and free agency.","published":"2022-04-09T11:31:33.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/buffalo-bills/post/_/id/37156/how-the-buffalo-bills-can-address-cornerback-in-bid-to-maintain-no-1-defense","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Alaina Getzenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Roger McCreary","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_McCreary","description":"American football player (born 2000)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:33:48Z","intro":"Roger Lee McCreary (born February 10, 2000) is an American professional football cornerback for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Auburn Tigers. McCreary was drafted by the Tennessee Titans in the second round of the 2022 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"McCreary attended Williamson High School in Mobile, Alabama. Coming out of high school, McCreary was a 3 star prospect and was the 87th ranked cornerback. He committed to Auburn University to play college football after de-committing from South Alabama."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"McCreary played in seven games as a true freshman at Auburn in 2018. He played in all 13 games in 2019, recording 36 tackles and one interception. McCreary became a full time starter during his junior year in 2020. In 10 games, he had 45 tackles and three interceptions. \nHe returned to Auburn for his senior year in 2021, rather than enter the 2021 NFL draft. In 2021, McCreary recorded 49 tackles, two interceptions and an SEC best 14 pass breakups. Following his senior season, McCreary was named as a First-team All-American by both the Associated Press and ESPN, as well as being selected consensus First-team All-SEC by both coaches and the AP."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"TENNESSEE TITANS\nThe Tennessee Titans selected McCreary in the second round (35th overall) of the 2022 NFL draft. He was the fifth cornerback selected.\nHe started all 17 games in his rookie season, finishing with 84 total tackles, one interception, and eight passes defensed. McCreary also helped force a notable turnover on Week 15 against the Los Angeles Chargers, by jumping out of bounds to tip a pass mid-air by Justin Herbert, which was received by Joshua Kalu for an assisted interception.\nMcCreary moved into the starting nickelback position for the 2023 season. He played in 15 games with 11 starts, recording 86 tackles, two sacks, six passes defensed, one interception, and a forced fumble.\nDuring the 2024 season, McCreary appeared in 15 games, recording 50 tackles, a pass deflection, three pressures, and a sack.\n\nLOS ANGELES RAMS\nOn October 27, 2025, McCreary and a conditional 2026 sixth-round pick were traded to the Los Angeles Rams in exchange for a conditional fifth-round pick. He was placed on injured reserve on November 26 after suffering a hip injury in Week 12 against the Tampa Bay Buccaneers. McCreary was activated on December 29, ahead of the team's Week 17 matchup against the Atlanta Falcons.\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn March 13, 2026, McCreary signed with the Detroit Lions on a one-year contract."},{"key":"personal","title":"Personal life","text":"McCreary's pregame meal is two plates of baked beans with eight packets of sugar."}],"wikidataId":"Q108928596","family":[{"relation":"Relative","name":"Angelo James","description":"football player (born 1962)"}],"social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-03-16","text":"Signed DB Roger McCreary, LB Malcolm Rodriguez and DB Rock Ya-Sin."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4371973","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/M/McCrRo01.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/roger-mccreary/83176","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/roger-mccreary/10080","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_McCreary"},"insights":["Ranks 7th of 107 qualified cornerbacks in passes defended.","Ranks 11th of 112 qualified cornerbacks in missed-tackle %.","On the field for 75% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $1.3M is the 31st-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season."]}